  ],
  "description": "Type B, engaged mono channel from the archived TL072 / LM13700 schematic with the 47 kΩ Drive and dual Tune controls. SW101 has linked −10 and 0 dB operating-level positions. The tuned high-pass filter drives both a full-wave limiter detector and the OTA generator, whose bias current contains an audio component. The LM13700 section uses a CA3080 matched-pair equivalent, external linearizing diodes and a unity follower with 6.8 Ω output resistance for the high-impedance Darlington buffer. R108 is 150 Ω following Jatin Chowdhury’s Type B drive-stage simulation; the 150 kΩ inscription on the TL072 drawing yields negligible control range. C104 uses the 4.7 µF value from Christian’s 2003 Type B trace. U103 and D101–103 use the equivalent full-wave peak detector: opposite-polarity unity taps feed matched 1N914s into C114 through 1 kΩ. The limiter follower uses its closed-loop unity equivalent. Supplies are ±15 V. The display and bypass are omitted.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Drive",
      "Tune",
      "Mix"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Aphex Aural Exciter Type B",
